--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party dependencies and their licenses (verify against current upstream
terms before vendoring anything):

- SAM2 (Segment Anything 2)  — permissive (Apache-2.0/BSD-style). Used as an
  optional dependency for interactive mask tracking. Not vendored.
- RAFT (optical flow)        — permissive (BSD). Used as an optional dependency
  for flow estimation. Not vendored.
- PyAV / FFmpeg              — LGPL/BSD (FFmpeg components vary). Optional IO.
- OpenCV                     — Apache-2.0. Optional (homography fast path).
- PyTorch / TorchVision      — BSD. Optional (learned stages).

NON-PERMISSIVE — MUST NOT be vendored into this Apache-2.0 project:

- ProPainter, E2FGVI         — S-Lab non-commercial license. Referenced for
  design only; no code or weights are included.
- LaMa (`big-lama` weights)  — code and weights carry different terms. If the
  M1 residual path is wired to LaMa, it MUST remain behind the
  `vidfill.synthesis` interface and be flagged here as a non-permissive
  OPTIONAL dependency until replaced by an in-repo, permissively-trained model.

The completion network (flow/completion.py) and synthesis model
(synthesis/attention.py) are intended to be trained in-repo on permissively
licensed data (YouTube-VOS, DAVIS) rather than adapted from non-permissive
checkpoints. See docs/licensing.md.
